  ($cd$case-001$cd$, $cd$season-1$cd$, $cd$001$cd$, $cd$THE DUPLICATE REPORTS$cd$, $cd$The automated record system is duplicating critical case files. Every even-numbered report is being filed twice.$cd$, $cd$Find why the report buffer contains duplicates and repair the loop so every report is unique.$cd$, $cd$EASY$cd$, 250, null, $cd$["BRIEFING","LEARN","INVESTIGATE","CODE","EVIDENCE","SOLVE"]$cd$::jsonb, $cd$loops and conditions$cd$, $cd${"title":"LOOPS AND CONDITIONS","subtitle":"Your investigation points toward a repeated action that should only happen once.","clue":"The same report is appended twice whenever the loop reaches an even value.","sections":[{"title":"LOOPS","description":"A loop repeats a block of code for each value in a sequence or until a condition changes."},{"title":"CONDITIONS","description":"A condition decides whether a block should run. If the condition is too broad, the block may execute when it should not."},{"title":"INVARIANTS","description":"An invariant is a rule that must remain true. Here, every report should appear exactly once."}],"hint":"Trace one even iteration carefully. Ask whether the same value is appended more than once."}$cd$::jsonb, $cd${"rootCause":"The loop appends the current report a second time when the value is even.","fixSummary":"Keep the single append inside the loop and remove the duplicate append branch.","beforeCode":"reports.append(r)\nif r % 2 == 0:\n    reports.append(r)","afterCode":"reports.append(r)","successMessage":"The corrected loop produces exactly five unique reports."}$cd$::jsonb),
  ($cd$case-002$cd$, $cd$season-1$cd$, $cd$002$cd$, $cd$THE MISSING DEPOSIT$cd$, $cd$The vault ledger reports less money than was deposited. One deposit vanishes every night — always the first one.$cd$, $cd$Find out why the vault total is short and fix the loop so every deposit is counted.$cd$, $cd$MEDIUM$cd$, 300, $cd$case-001$cd$, $cd$["BRIEFING","LEARN","INVESTIGATE","CODE","EVIDENCE","SOLVE"]$cd$::jsonb, $cd$list indexing and range()$cd$, $cd${"title":"INDEXES AND RANGE","subtitle":"Your investigation points toward a loop that starts counting in the wrong place.","clue":"The missing amount always equals the very first deposit of the night.","sections":[{"title":"INDEX 0","description":"Python lists start counting at 0. The first item of a list lives at position 0, not 1."},{"title":"RANGE(A, B)","description":"range(a, b) produces a, a + 1, … up to b − 1. The start value is included; the end value is not."},{"title":"DIRECT LOOPS","description":"for item in items: walks every element without any index, so nothing can be skipped by accident."}],"hint":"Write down which indexes range(1, len(deposits)) produces for a list of five deposits."}$cd$::jsonb, $cd${"rootCause":"The loop starts at index 1, so the deposit at index 0 is never added to the total.","fixSummary":"Start the range at 0 — or loop over the deposits directly — so every deposit is counted.","beforeCode":"for i in range(1, len(deposits)):\n    total += deposits[i]","afterCode":"for amount in deposits:\n    total += amount","successMessage":"Every deposit is counted and the vault total balances."}$cd$::jsonb),
  ($cd$case-003$cd$, $cd$season-1$cd$, $cd$003$cd$, $cd$THE CASE-SENSITIVE SUSPECT$cd$, $cd$Known suspects are walking straight past the watchlist scanner. The scanner only flags names typed in lowercase.$cd$, $cd$Fix the scanner so suspects are flagged no matter how their names are capitalised.$cd$, $cd$MEDIUM$cd$, 350, $cd$case-002$cd$, $cd$["BRIEFING","LEARN","INVESTIGATE","CODE","EVIDENCE","SOLVE"]$cd$::jsonb, $cd$string normalisation$cd$, $cd${"title":"COMPARING STRINGS","subtitle":"Your investigation points toward two names that look the same to people but not to Python.","clue":"Every suspect who slipped through had a capital letter in their name.","sections":[{"title":"CASE MATTERS","description":"\"Moriarty\" == \"moriarty\" is False — uppercase and lowercase letters are different characters."},{"title":".STRIP()","description":"Returns a copy of the string without spaces at the start and end."},{"title":".LOWER()","description":"Returns a copy of the string in lowercase, so differently-typed names compare equal."}],"hint":"Print each name right before it is checked against the watchlist. Does it look exactly like the watchlist entry?"}$cd$::jsonb, $cd${"rootCause":"Names were compared exactly as typed, but the watchlist stores every name in lowercase.","fixSummary":"Normalise each name with .strip().lower() before checking it against the watchlist.","beforeCode":"name = name.strip()\nif name in watchlist:","afterCode":"name = name.strip().lower()\nif name in watchlist:","successMessage":"Every suspect is flagged, however their name was typed."}$cd$::jsonb)
